Several builtins here follow uutils (coreutils, diffutils, util-linux; MIT) or toybox (0BSD) closely;
each file names its source in its header. License texts: ../../THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md

F08 copy/link/move regression scenarios reference:
- Toybox tests/cp.test, 6a0c0ef5eeb2c43e4feef9781398c1718b8bddcb, 0BSD.
- uutils/coreutils tests/by-util/test_ln.rs and test_mv.rs,
  fee61ff5d4f87e0f912a52e639942b5f7ad58663, MIT.
The environment reference-conflict audit also checked test_env.rs at that pin.
F08 implementations and regression tests are native Go; no upstream algorithm
or fixture bytes were imported. Local adapter fixture provenance is recorded
separately in tests/provenance/fixtures.json.

U13 chgrp and U14 install follow:
- Toybox toys/posix/chgrp.c and toys/posix/cp.c (install), 6a0c0ef5eeb2c43e4feef9781398c1718b8bddcb, 0BSD.
- Toybox tests/chgrp.test (case list and placements ported to tests/native) and
  tests/install.test (copied verbatim to tests/toybox/install.test) at that pin.
- uutils/coreutils src/uu/chgrp, src/uu/install, tests/by-util/test_chgrp.rs and
  tests/by-util/test_install.rs, fee61ff5d4f87e0f912a52e639942b5f7ad58663, MIT.
Both implementations and their native tests are original Go: option sets,
message wording and case placement follow the references, no upstream source or
fixture bytes were copied. install -s is rejected by design and never runs an
external strip program.
